IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), piece er2 (regulations 19 to 34): SMALL HELPERS shared by the er2 modules.
-- Nothing here is law: each helper is arithmetic on days that two or more er2 modules need (the later of two days, the days two
-- periods share). They carry no @ref because no provision states them. Every name begins `er2 ` so that, after the merge,
-- no other piece can define the same name.
-- Dates are built with YMD from eia-core; a period is the core's Period of days (both ends included).

§ `Helpers on days and periods`

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `er2 the later of two days` IS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `er2 the earlier of two days` IS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- The number of days (ends included) that two periods have in common; 0 when they share none.
GIVEN p IS A `Period of days`
      q IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `er2 the number of days two periods have in common` IS
    IF   Day `the last shared day` LESS THAN Day `the first shared day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE (Day `the last shared day` MINUS Day `the first shared day`) PLUS 1
    WHERE
        `the first shared day` MEANS `er2 the later of two days` (p's `first day of the period`) (q's `first day of the period`)
        `the last shared day` MEANS `er2 the earlier of two days` (p's `last day of the period`) (q's `last day of the period`)

-- The inner period lies wholly within the outer one (ends included).
GIVEN inner IS A `Period of days`
      outer IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `er2 a period lies wholly within another` IF
        inner's `first day of the period` AT LEAST outer's `first day of the period`
    AND inner's `last day of the period` AT MOST outer's `last day of the period`

-- The week (Sunday to Saturday, s 2(1) "week") that contains a day, as a period.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `er2 the week containing the day` IS
    `Period of days` OF (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` d), (`s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` d)
